From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:12:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Count the Apple A9 as supported

The A9's GPU (BVNC 9.15.6.2) takes jobs now, so the driver binds to it
without powervr.exp_hw_support, as it does to the A10's: the GPU starts
on every boot of a board that enables its node.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index 0b6fd3c..2c06a4a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -539,12 +539,9 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 52, 104, 182):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(13, 10, 6, 2):	/* Apple A10 (T8010) */
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(9, 15, 6, 2):	/* Apple A9 (S8003) */
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
-	/* Apple A9 (S8003): its firmware is started, no job runs on it yet */
-	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(9, 15, 6, 2):
-		return PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL;
-
 	default:
 		return PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN;
 	}
